Subject: [PATCH] C14, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M20): A GATE ON
 THE PUBLIC FACE: THE PAGES A READER OUTSIDE THE PROJECT OPENS, AND THE INNER
 WORDS ON EACH, HELD AS FOUND AND ALLOWED ONLY TO FALL

Main's M20, at the owner's point of 2026-11-12 entered by main in plain words: the public face uses none of the
record's inner words, and a gate holds it, with planted cases both ways.

THE GATE, public-face, the 55th. It reads the pages of one list, PUBLIC_FACE, and counts on each the words of
main's list: owner, main as a person, cc, seat, lane, relay, ruling or ruled, card, and a session's name. A
possessive or a plural is counted as its word. "Main" in a phrase of plain English ("the main goal", "the main
result", and six more) is not counted, nor is "card" as the atlas query's subcommand.

THE LIST IS THE BUILDER'S READING OF M20, and main's to change: the README; the main goal; the knowledge index;
the pages the README's "start here" sends a newcomer to that are not the working record (the programme so far,
the plan of 2026-10-29, the vocabulary, the foundation); the two front pages of the plan (ROADMAP, MASTERPLAN);
the generated views a newcomer is sent to; the workdesk's README; and of papers/ the paper itself and the README
of its verification package. Not on it: the logs, the register, the status page, the seats' pages, the arcs,
and the verdict ledger and the spine, which are named in the gate as working indices.

HELD AS FOUND: 1,456 words on the 17 pages (built again on main's fe146ca49, where main landed this card's second patch and the README is at zero), by page and by word, written into the gate. A count may only fall,
and a word that is new on a page fails even if another word left it in the same commit. So the gate lands
green, and the series lowers each page to zero, one patch at a time. Three pages are at zero on this base: the README, the
coverage view and the ledger of walls.

THE TESTS. tests/test_public_face.py, four tests: the words counted and not counted (words inside other words;
the plain-English "main"); a new word fails where another left the page, a rise fails, a fall passes, a missing
page fails; the working record and the working indices are not on the list; and on this repository the gate
passes and the held table is today's count. The failing-path test, in tests/test_gate_failing_paths.py: "the
owner" put into the README fails; the same words in the progress log and in the verdict ledger pass.

Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
